/* Verse Games: THE WHOLE COUNSEL · 1 Samuel chapters 26-30
   Verse text is filled/verified from the KJV by tools/fill-verses.js */
VG.registerBibleChapters("1samuel", [
{n:26, name:"David Spares Saul Again", seal:{ref:"1 Samuel 26:23",verse:"The LORD render to every man his righteousness and his faithfulness: for the LORD delivered thee into my hand to day, but I would not stretch forth mine hand against the LORD’S anointed."}, facts:["Did you know the Ziphites betrayed David to Saul twice, first in 1 Samuel 23 and again here at the hill of Hachilah (1 Samuel 26:1)?","Did you know Abishai offered to pin Saul to the ground with a single spear thrust, and David refused, leaving Saul's fate in the LORD's hands (1 Samuel 26:8-10)?","Did you know Saul finally confessed, 'I have played the fool, and have erred exceedingly,' yet still did not repent (1 Samuel 26:21)?"], questions:[
{q:"Who came to Saul at Gibeah to betray David?", options:["The Ziphites","The Keilites","The men of Jabesh","The elders of Hebron"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 26:1",verse:"And the Ziphites came unto Saul to Gibeah, saying, Doth not David hide himself in the hill of Hachilah, which is before Jeshimon?", insight:"The Ziphites told Saul where David hid; betrayal by neighbors cuts deeper than the sword of enemies."},
{q:"How many chosen men of Israel did Saul take to seek David?", options:["Three thousand","Three hundred","Thirty thousand","One hundred"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 26:2",verse:"Then Saul arose, and went down to the wilderness of Ziph, having three thousand chosen men of Israel with him, to seek David in the wilderness of Ziph.", insight:"Three thousand chosen men to hunt one shepherd; envy spends fortunes to chase what it cannot catch."},
{q:"Where did Saul pitch his camp?", options:["On the hill of Hachilah, before Jeshimon","In the valley of Elah","At the gates of Gibeah","On Mount Gilboa"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 26:3",verse:"And Saul pitched in the hill of Hachilah, which is before Jeshimon, by the way. But David abode in the wilderness, and he saw that Saul came after him into the wilderness.", insight:"Saul pitched on the hill of Hachilah, close enough to hear his own spear taken; sinners often sleep within reach of grace."},
{q:"How did David learn that Saul had truly come against him?", options:["He sent out spies","A dream told him","Saul's men warned him","Abner confessed it"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 26:4",verse:"David therefore sent out spies, and understood that Saul was come in very deed.", insight:"David sent out spies before acting; wisdom verifies the threat before it answers it."},
{q:"Who was the captain of Saul's host?", options:["Abner the son of Ner","Joab the son of Zeruiah","Benaiah the son of Jehoiada","Asahel the son of Zeruiah"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 26:5",verse:"And David arose, and came to the place where Saul had pitched: and David beheld the place where Saul lay, and Abner the son of Ner, the captain of his host: and Saul lay in the trench, and the people pitched round about him.", insight:"Abner lay with his people around the king, yet all of them slept; human guards fail where God's watch succeeds."},
{q:"Whom did David ask, 'Who will go down with me to Saul to the camp?'", options:["Ahimelech the Hittite, and Abishai the son of Zeruiah","Joab and Asahel","Abiathar the priest","Two of his mighty men"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 26:6",verse:"Then answered David and said to Ahimelech the Hittite, and to Abishai the son of Zeruiah, brother to Joab, saying, Who will go down with me to Saul to the camp? And Abishai said, I will go down with thee.", insight:"David invited companions into danger but kept the moral choice his own; leaders take counsel and own the decision."},
{q:"Who went down with David into Saul's camp by night?", options:["Abishai the son of Zeruiah","Ahimelech the Hittite","Joab the son of Zeruiah","Abiathar the priest"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 26:7",verse:"So David and Abishai came to the people by night: and, behold, Saul lay sleeping within the trench, and his spear stuck in the ground at his bolster: but Abner and the people lay round about him.", insight:"Abishai went down with David into the sleeping camp; courage shared is courage doubled."},
{q:"What did Abishai offer to do to the sleeping Saul?", options:["Smite him with the spear even to the earth at once, and not the second time","Cut off his head with his own sword","Bind him and bring him to David","Set the camp on fire"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 26:8",verse:"Then said Abishai to David, God hath delivered thine enemy into thine hand this day: now therefore let me smite him, I pray thee, with the spear even to the earth at once, and I will not smite him the second time.", insight:"Abishai saw a finished enemy; David saw the LORD's anointed. Righteous men can read the same moment two ways."},
{q:"How did David answer Abishai?", options:["Destroy him not; for who can stretch forth his hand against the LORD's anointed, and be guiltless?","Take him now, for God has delivered him","Bind him, but spare his life","Wait until he wakes, then fight him fairly"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 26:9",verse:"And David said to Abishai, Destroy him not: for who can stretch forth his hand against the LORD’S anointed, and be guiltless?", insight:"'Who can stretch forth his hand against the LORD's anointed, and be guiltless?' Reverence for God's appointed restrains even justified anger."},
{q:"What did David say the LORD would do with Saul?", options:["The LORD shall smite him; or his day shall come to die; or he shall descend into battle, and perish","The LORD would bless him forever","The LORD had forgotten him","The LORD would make him David's servant"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 26:10",verse:"David said furthermore, As the LORD liveth, the LORD shall smite him; or his day shall come to die; or he shall descend into battle, and perish.", insight:"David left Saul's end to the LORD, in His time and His way; vengeance surrendered is faith matured."},
{q:"What did David take from Saul's bolster?", options:["The spear and the cruse of water","The crown and the bracelet","The sword and the shield","The robe and the sandals"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 26:11",verse:"The LORD forbid that I should stretch forth mine hand against the LORD’S anointed: but, I pray thee, take thou now the spear that is at his bolster, and the cruse of water, and let us go.", insight:"David took the spear and the water, proof not plunder; mercy gathers evidence, not trophies."},
{q:"Why did no one in the camp see, know, or wake?", options:["Because a deep sleep from the LORD was fallen upon them","Because David drugged their wine","Because the guards had fled","Because a storm drowned all sound"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 26:12",verse:"So David took the spear and the cruse of water from Saul’s bolster; and they gat them away, and no man saw it, nor knew it, neither awaked: for they were all asleep; because a deep sleep from the LORD was fallen upon them.", insight:"A deep sleep from the LORD covered the camp; when God fights for you, He first quiets the field."},
{q:"Where did David stand to call out to the camp?", options:["On the top of an hill afar off","In the trench beside Saul","At the gates of Gibeah","On the plain of Ziph"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 26:13",verse:"Then David went over to the other side, and stood on the top of an hill afar off; a great space being between them:", insight:"David stood afar off with a great space between them; the godly keep distance from the quarrel they refuse to join."},
{q:"Whom did David mock for failing to guard the king?", options:["Abner","Joab","The Ziphites","Saul's armor bearer"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 26:15",verse:"And David said to Abner, Art not thou a valiant man? and who is like to thee in Israel? wherefore then hast thou not kept thy lord the king? for there came one of the people in to destroy the king thy lord.", insight:"David asked Abner, 'Art not thou a valiant man?' Faithfulness to duty is the guard's honor, and its lapse is shame."},
{q:"What did David say Abner and his men deserved?", options:["They were worthy to die, because they had not kept their master","A public rebuke before the army","Exile from the king's service","A fine of silver"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 26:16",verse:"This thing is not good that thou hast done. As the LORD liveth, ye are worthy to die, because ye have not kept your master, the LORD’S anointed. And now see where the king’s spear is, and the cruse of water that was at his bolster.", insight:"'Ye are worthy to die,' said David to sleeping guards; vigilance is a debt we owe those we protect."},
{q:"What did Saul say when he knew David's voice?", options:["Is this thy voice, my son David?","Why have you stolen my spear?","Bring me Abner at once","Sound the alarm to battle"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 26:17",verse:"And Saul knew David’s voice, and said, Is this thy voice, my son David? And David said, It is my voice, my lord, O king.", insight:"'Is this thy voice, my son David?' Even a king who hunts him still calls him son; guilt remembers affection."},
{q:"What question did David put to Saul?", options:["Wherefore doth my lord thus pursue after his servant? for what have I done?","When wilt thou make me captain of thy host?","Why hast thou taken my wives away?","How long wilt thou hide in Gibeah?"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 26:18",verse:"And he said, Wherefore doth my lord thus pursue after his servant? for what have I done? or what evil is in mine hand?", insight:"'What have I done?' David pleaded innocence with a clear conscience; the clean-handed can ask the hard question."},
{q:"How did David describe Saul's pursuit of him?", options:["The king of Israel is come out to seek a flea, as when one doth hunt a partridge in the mountains","A lion hunting a lamb in the thicket","An eagle stooping on a dove","A shepherd chasing a lost sheep"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 26:20",verse:"Now therefore, let not my blood fall to the earth before the face of the LORD: for the king of Israel is come out to seek a flea, as when one doth hunt a partridge in the mountains.", insight:"A flea, a partridge: David shrank the threat to its true size; fear flees when we name it plainly."},
{q:"What did Saul confess to David?", options:["I have sinned: I have played the fool, and have erred exceedingly","I was right to pursue thee all these years","Abner forced me to come","God has forsaken me forever"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 26:21",verse:"Then said Saul, I have sinned: return, my son David: for I will no more do thee harm, because my soul was precious in thine eyes this day: behold, I have played the fool, and have erred exceedingly.", insight:"'I have played the fool' is a true confession; its tragedy is that Saul spoke it and changed nothing."},
{q:"What blessing did Saul pronounce over David?", options:["Blessed be thou, my son David: thou shalt both do great things, and also shalt still prevail","The kingdom shall return to my house","Go, and be my captain forever","The LORD bless thee in Gath"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 26:25",verse:"Then Saul said to David, Blessed be thou, my son David: thou shalt both do great things, and also shalt still prevail. So David went on his way, and Saul returned to his place.", insight:"Even Saul foresaw David's prevailing; God's purposes speak through the lips of enemies."}
]},
{n:27, name:"David Flees to Gath", seal:{ref:"1 Samuel 27:4",verse:"And it was told Saul that David was fled to Gath: and he sought no more again for him."}, facts:["Did you know David fled to Achish king of Gath with six hundred men, and Achish gave him Ziklag, which afterward belonged to the kings of Judah (1 Samuel 27:2,6)?","Did you know David lived in the country of the Philistines a full year and four months, all while secretly raiding Israels old enemies (1 Samuel 27:7-8)?","Did you know David told Achish he was raiding the south of Judah, when he was really wiping out the Geshurites, the Gezrites, and the Amalekites, leaving no survivors to tell (1 Samuel 27:10-11)?"], questions:[
{q:"What did David say in his heart as he fled Saul?", options:["I shall now perish one day by the hand of Saul","The LORD will make me king tomorrow","Saul will surely repent","I will hide in the caves forever"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 27:1",verse:"And David said in his heart, I shall now perish one day by the hand of Saul: there is nothing better for me than that I should speedily escape into the land of the Philistines; and Saul shall despair of me, to seek me any more in any coast of Israel: so shall I escape out of his hand.", insight:"'I shall now perish' was the fear of a weary heart, not a prophecy; weariness whispers lies that faith must answer."},
{q:"What plan did David settle on to escape Saul?", options:["To escape speedily into the land of the Philistines","To hide in the wilderness of Judah","To sail across the sea","To seek refuge in Egypt"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 27:1",verse:"And David said in his heart, I shall now perish one day by the hand of Saul: there is nothing better for me than that I should speedily escape into the land of the Philistines; and Saul shall despair of me, to seek me any more in any coast of Israel: so shall I escape out of his hand.", insight:"David fled to the Philistines, his enemies, for safety; desperation sometimes seeks shelter in strange places."},
{q:"How many men passed over with David to Achish?", options:["Six hundred","Three hundred","Three thousand","Four hundred"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 27:2",verse:"And David arose, and he passed over with the six hundred men that were with him unto Achish, the son of Maoch, king of Gath.", insight:"Six hundred loyal men followed David into exile; faithful company is God's provision in hard seasons."},
{q:"To whom did David go in Gath?", options:["Achish the son of Maoch, king of Gath","The priests of Dagon","The lords of the Philistines","The elders of Gath"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 27:2",verse:"And David arose, and he passed over with the six hundred men that were with him unto Achish, the son of Maoch, king of Gath.", insight:"David served Achish, once his enemy's king; God can place His servants in unlikely courts."},
{q:"Which two wives were with David at Gath?", options:["Ahinoam the Jezreelitess, and Abigail the Carmelitess","Michal and Maacah","Haggith and Abital","Eglah and Bathsheba"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 27:3",verse:"And David dwelt with Achish at Gath, he and his men, every man with his household, even David with his two wives, Ahinoam the Jezreelitess, and Abigail the Carmelitess, Nabal’s wife.", insight:"Ahinoam and Abigail shared David's exile; faithfulness in marriage walks through the wilderness too."},
{q:"What did Saul do when he was told David had fled to Gath?", options:["He sought no more again for him","He gathered his army and pursued","He made a treaty with Achish","He wept and repented"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 27:4",verse:"And it was told Saul that David was fled to Gath: and he sought no more again for him.", insight:"Saul sought no more when David crossed the border; God used even flight to still the pursuit."},
{q:"What did David ask of Achish?", options:["A place in some town in the country, that he might dwell there","The throne of Gath","Ships to sail home","A field near the palace"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 27:5",verse:"And David said unto Achish, If I have now found grace in thine eyes, let them give me a place in some town in the country, that I may dwell there: for why should thy servant dwell in the royal city with thee?", insight:"David asked for a country town, not the royal city; the humble request often wins what boldness cannot."},
{q:"What place did Achish give to David?", options:["Ziklag","Hebron","Keilah","Jarmuth"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 27:6",verse:"Then Achish gave him Ziklag that day: wherefore Ziklag pertaineth unto the kings of Judah unto this day.", insight:"Achish gave David Ziklag that day; God's gifts sometimes arrive through pagan hands."},
{q:"To whom did Ziklag afterward belong?", options:["The kings of Judah","The priests of Nob","The sons of Saul","The lords of the Philistines"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 27:6",verse:"Then Achish gave him Ziklag that day: wherefore Ziklag pertaineth unto the kings of Judah unto this day.", insight:"Ziklag pertained to the kings of Judah; what seems a refugee's hut becomes a king's inheritance."},
{q:"How long did David dwell in the country of the Philistines?", options:["A full year and four months","Seven years","Forty days","Three years"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 27:7",verse:"And the time that David dwelt in the country of the Philistines was a full year and four months.", insight:"A full year and four months in exile; God's delays are measured, not forgotten."},
{q:"Whom did David and his men invade while dwelling with the Philistines?", options:["The Geshurites, and the Gezrites, and the Amalekites","The Moabites and the Ammonites","The Edomites and the Midianites","The Jebusites of Jerusalem"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 27:8",verse:"And David and his men went up, and invaded the Geshurites, and the Gezrites, and the Amalekites: for those nations were of old the inhabitants of the land, as thou goest to Shur, even unto the land of Egypt.", insight:"David warred on Israel's old enemies in secret; not all battles are fought in the open."},
{q:"How long had those nations inhabited the land?", options:["Of old, from Shur even unto the land of Egypt","Since the days of Abraham","Only a few years","Since Saul's reign"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 27:8",verse:"And David and his men went up, and invaded the Geshurites, and the Gezrites, and the Amalekites: for those nations were of old the inhabitants of the land, as thou goest to Shur, even unto the land of Egypt.", insight:"Those nations were of old the inhabitants; old evils do not die of age, they must be confronted."},
{q:"What did David take from those he smote?", options:["Sheep, and oxen, and asses, and camels, and apparel","Gold and silver only","Weapons of brass","Ships and chariots"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 27:9",verse:"And David smote the land, and left neither man nor woman alive, and took away the sheep, and the oxen, and the asses, and the camels, and the apparel, and returned, and came to Achish.", insight:"He took sheep, oxen, camels, and apparel; provision follows obedience, even in exile."},
{q:"What did David leave alive in the lands he smote?", options:["Neither man nor woman alive","The children and the elders","The priests and the craftsmen","The shepherds and their flocks"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 27:9",verse:"And David smote the land, and left neither man nor woman alive, and took away the sheep, and the oxen, and the asses, and the camels, and the apparel, and returned, and came to Achish.", insight:"He left neither man nor woman alive, lest they tell; in a pagan court, one leaked word could doom them all."},
{q:"What did David tell Achish he had raided?", options:["The south of Judah, and the south of the Jerahmeelites, and the south of the Kenites","The cities of the Philistines","The camp of Saul","The borders of Egypt"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 27:10",verse:"And Achish said, Whither have ye made a road to day? And David said, Against the south of Judah, and against the south of the Jerahmeelites, and against the south of the Kenites.", insight:"David said he raided Judah's south; deception in a deceitful court was survival, though not his finest hour."},
{q:"Why did David save none alive to bring tidings to Gath?", options:["Lest they should tell on them, saying, So did David","Because Achish commanded it","Because the law required it","Because they refused to surrender"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 27:11",verse:"And David saved neither man nor woman alive, to bring tidings to Gath, saying, Lest they should tell on us, saying, So did David, and so will be his manner all the while he dwelleth in the country of the Philistines.", insight:"'Lest they should tell on us'; David guarded his secret with severity, for the whole company hung on it."},
{q:"How long did David keep this manner of raiding?", options:["All the while he dwelt in the country of the Philistines","For forty days","Until Saul died","Only that one season"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 27:11",verse:"And David saved neither man nor woman alive, to bring tidings to Gath, saying, Lest they should tell on us, saying, So did David, and so will be his manner all the while he dwelleth in the country of the Philistines.", insight:"So he did all the while he dwelt there; consistency in a hard place is quiet faithfulness."},
{q:"What did Achish believe about David?", options:["He hath made his people Israel utterly to abhor him; therefore he shall be my servant for ever","He was plotting to kill the king","He planned to return to Saul","He was a spy for Israel"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 27:12",verse:"And Achish believed David, saying, He hath made his people Israel utterly to abhor him; therefore he shall be my servant for ever.", insight:"Achish believed David was his forever; God let the enemy's trust shelter His anointed."},
{q:"What service did Achish expect from David?", options:["He shall be my servant for ever","One year of tribute","A single battle","The ransom of Ziklag"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 27:12",verse:"And Achish believed David, saying, He hath made his people Israel utterly to abhor him; therefore he shall be my servant for ever.", insight:"'He shall be my servant for ever,' said Achish; men claim forever what God has only lent for a season."},
{q:"What made Saul stop seeking David?", options:["David had fled to Gath, beyond Saul's reach","David had died in the wilderness","Achish had made peace with Saul","Samuel had returned from the dead"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 27:4",verse:"And it was told Saul that David was fled to Gath: and he sought no more again for him.", insight:"Flight to Gath stilled Saul's pursuit; sometimes God grants rest through the very road we feared."}
]},
{n:28, name:"Saul and the Medium at Endor", seal:{ref:"1 Samuel 28:19",verse:"Moreover the LORD will also deliver Israel with thee into the hand of the Philistines: and to morrow shalt thou and thy sons be with me: the LORD also shall deliver the host of Israel into the hand of the Philistines."}, facts:["Did you know Saul had banished all mediums and wizards from the land, yet in his desperation he disguised himself to consult one at Endor (1 Samuel 28:3,8)?","Did you know Samuel's message to Saul was a rebuke, not comfort: the LORD is departed from thee, and is become thine enemy (1 Samuel 28:16)?","Did you know the woman of Endor killed her own fat calf and baked unleavened bread to strengthen the fainting king for his last journey (1 Samuel 28:24)?"], questions:[
{q:"What did Achish require of David when the Philistines gathered for war?", options:["Thou shalt go out with me to battle, thou and thy men","Guard Ziklag while I fight","Pay tribute of gold","Stay in Gath and pray"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 28:1",verse:"And it came to pass in those days, that the Philistines gathered their armies together for warfare, to fight with Israel. And Achish said unto David, Know thou assuredly, that thou shalt go out with me to battle, thou and thy men.", insight:"'Thou shalt go out with me to battle'; David's deception placed him in an impossible loyalty."},
{q:"What did Achish promise to make David?", options:["Keeper of mine head for ever","Captain of a thousand","Priest of Dagon","Lord of Ziklag"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 28:2",verse:"And David said to Achish, Surely thou shalt know what thy servant can do. And Achish said to David, Therefore will I make thee keeper of mine head for ever.", insight:"Achish made David keeper of his head; trust from the wrong master is a snare, not an honor."},
{q:"What had become of Samuel?", options:["He was dead, and all Israel had lamented him, and buried him in Ramah","He had fled to the wilderness","He was hiding in a cave","He had joined the Philistines"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 28:3",verse:"Now Samuel was dead, and all Israel had lamented him, and buried him in Ramah, even in his own city. And Saul had put away those that had familiar spirits, and the wizards, out of the land.", insight:"Samuel was dead and buried in Ramah; when God's voice falls silent, men seek voices in the dark."},
{q:"What had Saul done with those who had familiar spirits and the wizards?", options:["He had put them away out of the land","He had made them his counselors","He had paid them tribute","He had sent them to Endor"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 28:3",verse:"Now Samuel was dead, and all Israel had lamented him, and buried him in Ramah, even in his own city. And Saul had put away those that had familiar spirits, and the wizards, out of the land.", insight:"Saul once banished the mediums; compromise in law brings collapse in life."},
{q:"Where did the Philistines pitch, and where did Saul pitch?", options:["The Philistines in Shunem, and Saul in Gilboa","The Philistines in Aphek, and Saul in Jezreel","The Philistines in Gath, and Saul in Ziklag","The Philistines in Ekron, and Saul in Ramah"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 28:4",verse:"And the Philistines gathered themselves together, and came and pitched in Shunem: and Saul gathered all Israel together, and they pitched in Gilboa.", insight:"Shunem against Gilboa; the armies gathered, and the forsaken king trembled."},
{q:"How did Saul feel when he saw the host of the Philistines?", options:["He was afraid, and his heart greatly trembled","He was filled with courage","He laughed with scorn","He fell asleep in peace"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 28:5",verse:"And when Saul saw the host of the Philistines, he was afraid, and his heart greatly trembled.", insight:"His heart greatly trembled; a conscience unrepentant cannot stand steady in battle."},
{q:"How did the LORD answer when Saul enquired of Him?", options:["The LORD answered him not, neither by dreams, nor by Urim, nor by prophets","With a voice of thunder","By a dream of victory","Through the priests of Nob"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 28:6",verse:"And when Saul enquired of the LORD, the LORD answered him not, neither by dreams nor by Urim, nor by prophets.", insight:"The LORD answered him not; silence from heaven is the heaviest answer of all."},
{q:"What did Saul ask his servants to find for him?", options:["A woman that hath a familiar spirit, that he might go and enquire of her","A prophet to anoint a new king","A captain to replace Abner","A priest to offer sacrifice"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 28:7",verse:"Then said Saul unto his servants, Seek me a woman that hath a familiar spirit, that I may go to her, and enquire of her. And his servants said to him, Behold, there is a woman that hath a familiar spirit at Endor.", insight:"'Seek me a woman that hath a familiar spirit'; the king who silenced God's voice now seeks forbidden ones."},
{q:"How did Saul go to the woman?", options:["He disguised himself, put on other raiment, with two men, and came by night","Openly with his whole army","As a beggar at noon","With Abner and his guard"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 28:8",verse:"And Saul disguised himself, and put on other raiment, and he went, and two men with him, and they came to the woman by night: and he said, I pray thee, divine unto me by the familiar spirit, and bring me him up, whom I shall name unto thee.", insight:"He came disguised by night; sin hides its face even while seeking counsel."},
{q:"What did Saul ask the woman to do?", options:["Divine unto me by the familiar spirit, and bring me up him whom I shall name","Tell his fortune for the battle","Curse David and his men","Bless the host of Israel"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 28:8",verse:"And Saul disguised himself, and put on other raiment, and he went, and two men with him, and they came to the woman by night: and he said, I pray thee, divine unto me by the familiar spirit, and bring me him up, whom I shall name unto thee.", insight:"'Bring me him up, whom I shall name'; forbidden help always names its price too late."},
{q:"What did the woman fear when Saul made his request?", options:["That he was laying a snare for her life, since Saul had cut off the mediums","That the spirit would not come","That her neighbors would hear","That the night was too dark"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 28:9",verse:"And the woman said unto him, Behold, thou knowest what Saul hath done, how he hath cut off those that have familiar spirits, and the wizards, out of the land: wherefore then layest thou a snare for my life, to cause me to die?", insight:"She feared a snare for her life; even the wicked know the law they break."},
{q:"What did Saul swear to the woman?", options:["As the LORD liveth, there shall no punishment happen to thee for this thing","He would make her rich","He would protect her house forever","He would repeal his own law"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 28:10",verse:"And Saul sware to her by the LORD, saying, As the LORD liveth, there shall no punishment happen to thee for this thing.", insight:"He swore by the LORD to protect a sin; oaths cannot sanctify disobedience."},
{q:"Whom did Saul ask the woman to bring up?", options:["Samuel","His father Kish","The prophet Gad","King David"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 28:11",verse:"Then said the woman, Whom shall I bring up unto thee? And he said, Bring me up Samuel.", insight:"'Bring me up Samuel'; the dead prophet was sought because the living God was refused."},
{q:"What did the woman do when she saw Samuel?", options:["She cried with a loud voice","She fell silent","She laughed","She fled from the house"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 28:12",verse:"And when the woman saw Samuel, she cried with a loud voice: and the woman spake to Saul, saying, Why hast thou deceived me? for thou art Saul.", insight:"She cried with a loud voice; what she summoned terrified the summoner."},
{q:"What did the woman say she saw?", options:["Gods ascending out of the earth","A pillar of fire","Angels with swords","A star falling"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 28:13",verse:"And the king said unto her, Be not afraid: for what sawest thou? And the woman said unto Saul, I saw gods ascending out of the earth.", insight:"'Gods ascending out of the earth'; the counterfeit always rises from below, never descends from above."},
{q:"How did the woman describe the figure she saw?", options:["An old man cometh up; and he is covered with a mantle","A young warrior with a spear","A priest in white linen","A king with a crown"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 28:14",verse:"And he said unto her, What form is he of? And she said, An old man cometh up; and he is covered with a mantle. And Saul perceived that it was Samuel, and he stooped with his face to the ground, and bowed himself.", insight:"An old man in a mantle; Saul knew the form, and bowed to a voice that would judge him."},
{q:"What did Saul confess to Samuel?", options:["I am sore distressed; the Philistines make war, and God is departed from me, and answereth me no more","I have repented of all my sins","David has taken my kingdom","The people have forsaken me"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 28:15",verse:"And Samuel said to Saul, Why hast thou disquieted me, to bring me up? And Saul answered, I am sore distressed; for the Philistines make war against me, and God is departed from me, and answereth me no more, neither by prophets, nor by dreams: therefore I have called thee, that thou mayest make known unto me what I shall do.", insight:"'God is departed from me'; Saul named his true loss at last, but sought remedy in the wrong place."},
{q:"What did Samuel say the LORD had become to Saul?", options:["The LORD is departed from thee, and is become thine enemy","The LORD would forgive him fully","The LORD had chosen Jonathan","The LORD would send rain"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 28:16",verse:"Then said Samuel, Wherefore then dost thou ask of me, seeing the LORD is departed from thee, and is become thine enemy?", insight:"'The LORD is become thine enemy'; the most dreadful sentence a soul can hear."},
{q:"What had the LORD done with the kingdom, according to Samuel?", options:["He had rent it out of Saul's hand, and given it to David","He had divided it among the tribes","He had given it to Jonathan","He had taken it to heaven"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 28:17",verse:"And the LORD hath done to him, as he spake by me: for the LORD hath rent the kingdom out of thine hand, and given it to thy neighbour, even to David:", insight:"The kingdom was rent away and given to David; disobedience forfeits what obedience would have kept."},
{q:"What did Samuel foretell for Saul and his sons?", options:["To morrow shalt thou and thy sons be with me","They would flee to Egypt","They would make peace with the Philistines","They would reign forty more years"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 28:19",verse:"Moreover the LORD will also deliver Israel with thee into the hand of the Philistines: and to morrow shalt thou and thy sons be with me: the LORD also shall deliver the host of Israel into the hand of the Philistines.", insight:"'To morrow shalt thou and thy sons be with me'; the last word Saul heard was the sentence he had earned."}
]},
{n:29, name:"The Philistines Reject David", seal:{ref:"1 Samuel 29:6",verse:"Then Achish called David, and said unto him, Surely, as the LORD liveth, thou hast been upright, and thy going out and thy coming in with me in the host is good in my sight: for I have not found evil in thee since the day of thy coming unto me unto this day: nevertheless the lords favour thee not."}, facts:["Did you know the Philistine princes quoted Israel's own victory song against David: 'Saul slew his thousands, and David his ten thousands' (1 Samuel 29:5)?","Did you know Achish swore 'as the LORD liveth' that David was upright, yet sent him away because the lords did not favor him (1 Samuel 29:6)?","Did you know God used the Philistines' suspicion to keep David from fighting against his own people Israel (1 Samuel 29:7-10)?"], questions:[
{q:"Where did the Philistines gather all their armies?", options:["To Aphek","To Gath","To Shunem","To Ekron"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 29:1",verse:"Now the Philistines gathered together all their armies to Aphek: and the Israelites pitched by a fountain which is in Jezreel.", insight:"The Philistines gathered to Aphek; great battles assemble long before the first sword is drawn."},
{q:"Where did the Israelites pitch?", options:["By a fountain which is in Jezreel","In the valley of Elah","At the gates of Gibeah","On Mount Gilboa"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 29:1",verse:"Now the Philistines gathered together all their armies to Aphek: and the Israelites pitched by a fountain which is in Jezreel.", insight:"Israel pitched by the fountain in Jezreel; even armies need water, and God provides it."},
{q:"How did the lords of the Philistines pass on?", options:["By hundreds, and by thousands","In single file","On horseback only","By night in secret"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 29:2",verse:"And the lords of the Philistines passed on by hundreds, and by thousands: but David and his men passed on in the rereward with Achish.", insight:"They passed by hundreds and by thousands; the proud display their strength before it fails them."},
{q:"Where were David and his men in the march?", options:["In the rereward with Achish","In the vanguard","Guarding the baggage","At the rear of Israel"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 29:2",verse:"And the lords of the Philistines passed on by hundreds, and by thousands: but David and his men passed on in the rereward with Achish.", insight:"David marched in the rereward with Achish; God was already working his way out of the trap."},
{q:"What did the princes of the Philistines ask?", options:["What do these Hebrews here?","Where is the king of Israel?","Who will fight Goliath?","When shall we return home?"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 29:3",verse:"Then said the princes of the Philistines, What do these Hebrews here? And Achish said unto the princes of the Philistines, Is not this David, the servant of Saul the king of Israel, which hath been with me these days, or these years, and I have found no fault in him since he fell unto me unto this day?", insight:"'What do these Hebrews here?' Suspicion asks the question that saves; not every door opened to us should be entered."},
{q:"What did Achish say he had found in David?", options:["No fault in him since he fell unto me unto this day","Great treasure and tribute","Secret letters to Saul","A plot against the Philistines"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 29:3",verse:"Then said the princes of the Philistines, What do these Hebrews here? And Achish said unto the princes of the Philistines, Is not this David, the servant of Saul the king of Israel, which hath been with me these days, or these years, and I have found no fault in him since he fell unto me unto this day?", insight:"Achish found no fault in David; a blameless life speaks even in a pagan court."},
{q:"What did the wroth princes command?", options:["Make this fellow return to his place","Slay David and his men","Send David to the front lines","Take David's wives as hostages"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 29:4",verse:"And the princes of the Philistines were wroth with him; and the princes of the Philistines said unto him, Make this fellow return, that he may go again to his place which thou hast appointed him, and let him not go down with us to battle, lest in the battle he be an adversary to us: for wherewith should he reconcile himself unto his master? should it not be with the heads of these men?", insight:"The princes demanded David's return; God can use unbelievers' fears to protect His servants."},
{q:"Why did the princes fear David in the battle?", options:["Lest he be an adversary to them, and reconcile himself to Saul with their heads","Lest he steal their spoil","Lest he worship his God openly","Lest he outshine their captains"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 29:4",verse:"And the princes of the Philistines were wroth with him; and the princes of the Philistines said unto him, Make this fellow return, that he may go again to his place which thou hast appointed him, and let him not go down with us to battle, lest in the battle he be an adversary to us: for wherewith should he reconcile himself unto his master? should it not be with the heads of these men?", insight:"They feared he would reconcile with his master at their cost; wise enemies respect divided loyalties."},
{q:"What song did the princes quote about David?", options:["Saul slew his thousands, and David his ten thousands","David has slain his ten thousands in Gath","Blessed be the king of Israel","The Philistines are fallen"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 29:5",verse:"Is not this David, of whom they sang one to another in dances, saying, Saul slew his thousands, and David his ten thousands?", insight:"They sang of David's ten thousands; old victories remembered can become present dangers."},
{q:"What did Achish swear about David?", options:["As the LORD liveth, thou hast been upright, and thy going out and thy coming in is good in my sight","By Dagon, thou art my servant","Thou shalt never leave Gath","I will make thee king"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 29:6",verse:"Then Achish called David, and said unto him, Surely, as the LORD liveth, thou hast been upright, and thy going out and thy coming in with me in the host is good in my sight: for I have not found evil in thee since the day of thy coming unto me unto this day: nevertheless the lords favour thee not.", insight:"Achish swore by the LORD that David was upright; truth forces testimony even from strange lips."},
{q:"What was Achish's only complaint against David?", options:["Nevertheless the lords favour thee not","Thou hast been lazy in service","Thy men are too few","Thou worshippest a strange God"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 29:6",verse:"Then Achish called David, and said unto him, Surely, as the LORD liveth, thou hast been upright, and thy going out and thy coming in with me in the host is good in my sight: for I have not found evil in thee since the day of thy coming unto me unto this day: nevertheless the lords favour thee not.", insight:"'The lords favour thee not'; favor with men is fickle, but David kept favor with God."},
{q:"What did Achish tell David to do?", options:["Return, and go in peace","Fight in the front rank","Bring thy wives to Gath","Swear loyalty to the Philistines"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 29:7",verse:"Wherefore now return, and go in peace, that thou displease not the lords of the Philistines.", insight:"'Return, and go in peace'; the dismissal David dreaded was the deliverance he needed."},
{q:"What did David ask Achish?", options:["What have I done? and what hast thou found in thy servant, that I may not go fight?","When shall we march to battle?","Where are my wages?","Why do the lords hate me?"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 29:8",verse:"And David said unto Achish, But what have I done? and what hast thou found in thy servant so long as I have been with thee unto this day, that I may not go fight against the enemies of my lord the king?", insight:"'What have I done?' David protested, not knowing God was answering his own prayer for a way out."},
{q:"How did Achish esteem David?", options:["Good in my sight, as an angel of God","As a servant of little worth","As a traitor to be watched","As a mercenary for hire"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 29:9",verse:"And Achish answered and said to David, I know that thou art good in my sight, as an angel of God: notwithstanding the princes of the Philistines have said, He shall not go up with us to the battle.", insight:"'As an angel of God'; a life of integrity shines, even to those who do not know the Lord."},
{q:"What had the princes decreed about David?", options:["He shall not go up with us to the battle","He shall lead the vanguard","He shall guard the baggage","He shall fight Goliath's brothers"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 29:9",verse:"And Achish answered and said to David, I know that thou art good in my sight, as an angel of God: notwithstanding the princes of the Philistines have said, He shall not go up with us to the battle.", insight:"'He shall not go up with us'; the closed door was God's hand, not man's rejection."},
{q:"When were David and his men to depart?", options:["Rise up early in the morning, and as soon as ye have light, depart","At midnight in secret","After the battle was won","On the seventh day"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 29:10",verse:"Wherefore now rise up early in the morning with thy master’s servants that are come with thee: and as soon as ye be up early in the morning, and have light, depart.", insight:"Rise early and depart at first light; when God opens the exit, do not linger."},
{q:"With whom was David to rise and depart?", options:["With thy master's servants that are come with thee","With Achish's guard","With the lords of the Philistines","Alone and unarmed"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 29:10",verse:"Wherefore now rise up early in the morning with thy master’s servants that are come with thee: and as soon as ye be up early in the morning, and have light, depart.", insight:"He departed with his master's servants; provision for the journey came through the very court that dismissed him."},
{q:"Where did David and his men go in the morning?", options:["To return into the land of the Philistines","To join Saul at Gilboa","To the wilderness of Judah","To the coast of Egypt"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 29:11",verse:"So David and his men rose up early to depart in the morning, to return into the land of the Philistines. And the Philistines went up to Jezreel.", insight:"They returned to the land of the Philistines, away from Israel's battle; God kept His anointed from lifting a sword against his own."},
{q:"Where did the Philistines go?", options:["Up to Jezreel","Down to Gath","Back to Aphek","Into the wilderness"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 29:11",verse:"So David and his men rose up early to depart in the morning, to return into the land of the Philistines. And the Philistines went up to Jezreel.", insight:"The Philistines went up to Jezreel, to the battle that would end Saul; David was spared its guilt."},
{q:"Why did Achish send David away in peace?", options:["That he might not displease the lords of the Philistines","Because David had sinned","Because Saul had paid a ransom","Because Achish feared David"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 29:7",verse:"Wherefore now return, and go in peace, that thou displease not the lords of the Philistines.", insight:"Achish sent him away to please the lords; behind men's politics, God was steering His servant clear."}
]},
{n:30, name:"Ziklag and the Spoil", seal:{ref:"1 Samuel 30:6",verse:"And David was greatly distressed; for the people spake of stoning him, because the soul of all the people was grieved, every man for his sons and for his daughters: but David encouraged himself in the LORD his God."}, facts:["Did you know the Amalekites burned Ziklag and carried off every woman and child, yet killed not one soul, great or small (1 Samuel 30:1-2)?","Did you know David's own men spoke of stoning him in their grief, and in that hour 'David encouraged himself in the LORD his God' (1 Samuel 30:6)?","Did you know David made it a standing law of Israel that the man who guards the baggage shares equally with the man who goes to battle (1 Samuel 30:24-25)?"], questions:[
{q:"When did David and his men come to Ziklag?", options:["On the third day","On the seventh day","At midnight","After forty days"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 30:1",verse:"And it came to pass, when David and his men were come to Ziklag on the third day, that the Amalekites had invaded the south, and Ziklag, and smitten Ziklag, and burned it with fire;", insight:"They came on the third day to find ashes; the hardest homecomings are the ones we never expected."},
{q:"What had the Amalekites done to Ziklag?", options:["Invaded the south, smitten Ziklag, and burned it with fire","Torn down its walls with engines","Poisoned its wells","Carried away its gates"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 30:1",verse:"And it came to pass, when David and his men were come to Ziklag on the third day, that the Amalekites had invaded the south, and Ziklag, and smitten Ziklag, and burned it with fire;", insight:"Ziklag lay burned with fire; ruin visits even the refuges God gives."},
{q:"Whom had the Amalekites taken captive?", options:["The women that were therein, great and small","The elders and the priests","The soldiers and their captains","The children only"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 30:2",verse:"And had taken the women captives, that were therein: they slew not any, either great or small, but carried them away, and went on their way.", insight:"They took the women captive, great and small; loss that touches family cuts deepest."},
{q:"How many of the captives did the Amalekites slay?", options:["They slew not any, either great or small","They slew every man","They slew the elders","They slew half of them"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 30:2",verse:"And had taken the women captives, that were therein: they slew not any, either great or small, but carried them away, and went on their way.", insight:"They slew not any; even in plunder, God's mercy set a limit on the enemy's cruelty."},
{q:"What did David and his men find when they came to the city?", options:["It was burned with fire; and their wives, sons, and daughters were taken captives","The gates standing open","The Amalekites still feasting","Their goods untouched"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 30:3",verse:"So David and his men came to the city, and, behold, it was burned with fire; and their wives, and their sons, and their daughters, were taken captives.", insight:"Burned city, captive families; sometimes obedience and disaster arrive in the same hour."},
{q:"What did David and the people do?", options:["Lifted up their voice and wept, until they had no more power to weep","Fled back to Gath","Cursed the Amalekites","Slept in the ashes"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 30:4",verse:"Then David and the people that were with him lifted up their voice and wept, until they had no more power to weep.", insight:"They wept until they had no more power to weep; grief emptied is grief God can fill."},
{q:"Which two wives of David were taken captive?", options:["Ahinoam the Jezreelitess, and Abigail the wife of Nabal the Carmelite","Michal and Maacah","Haggith and Abital","Eglah and Bathsheba"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 30:5",verse:"And David’s two wives were taken captives, Ahinoam the Jezreelitess, and Abigail the wife of Nabal the Carmelite.", insight:"Ahinoam and Abigail were taken; the leader's own house shared the people's loss."},
{q:"Why was David greatly distressed?", options:["The people spake of stoning him, because every man's soul was grieved","Saul had returned to pursue him","Achish had banished him","The Philistines demanded tribute"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 30:6",verse:"And David was greatly distressed; for the people spake of stoning him, because the soul of all the people was grieved, every man for his sons and for his daughters: but David encouraged himself in the LORD his God.", insight:"His own men spoke of stoning him; leaders sometimes bear the blame for losses they did not cause."},
{q:"What did David do in his distress?", options:["He encouraged himself in the LORD his God","He fled to the wilderness","He wept alone all night","He sent to Achish for help"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 30:6",verse:"And David was greatly distressed; for the people spake of stoning him, because the soul of all the people was grieved, every man for his sons and for his daughters: but David encouraged himself in the LORD his God.", insight:"'David encouraged himself in the LORD his God'; when no hand lifts you, learn to rise in Him."},
{q:"What did David ask Abiathar the priest to bring?", options:["The ephod","The ark of God","The sword of Goliath","The Urim and Thummim"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 30:7",verse:"And David said to Abiathar the priest, Ahimelech’s son, I pray thee, bring me hither the ephod. And Abiathar brought thither the ephod to David.", insight:"'Bring me hither the ephod'; before the sword, seek the counsel of God."},
{q:"What answer did the LORD give when David enquired?", options:["Pursue: for thou shalt surely overtake them, and without fail recover all","Wait until morning","Flee to the mountains","Make peace with the Amalekites"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 30:8",verse:"And David enquired at the LORD, saying, Shall I pursue after this troop? shall I overtake them? And he answered him, Pursue: for thou shalt surely overtake them, and without fail recover all.", insight:"'Pursue... without fail recover all'; God's promises are precise, and His word is sure."},
{q:"How many men went with David to the brook Besor?", options:["Six hundred","Three hundred","Four hundred","One thousand"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 30:9",verse:"So David went, he and the six hundred men that were with him, and came to the brook Besor, where those that were left behind stayed.", insight:"Six hundred set out; not all who start the pursuit finish it, and that is no shame."},
{q:"How many men were too faint to cross the brook Besor?", options:["Two hundred","One hundred","Fifty","Three hundred"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 30:10",verse:"But David pursued, he and four hundred men: for two hundred abode behind, which were so faint that they could not go over the brook Besor.", insight:"Two hundred abode behind, too faint to go on; weariness is not faithlessness."},
{q:"Whom did David's men find in the field?", options:["An Egyptian, servant to an Amalekite","A Philistine scout","A Hebrew shepherd","A wounded Amalekite captain"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 30:11",verse:"And they found an Egyptian in the field, and brought him to David, and gave him bread, and he did eat; and they made him drink water;", insight:"They found an Egyptian in the field; God plants guides on the road of obedience."},
{q:"How long had the Egyptian gone without bread or water?", options:["Three days and three nights","Seven days","Forty days","One day"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 30:12",verse:"And they gave him a piece of a cake of figs, and two clusters of raisins: and when he had eaten, his spirit came again to him: for he had eaten no bread, nor drunk any water, three days and three nights.", insight:"Three days without food; kindness to a stranger became the key to the whole campaign."},
{q:"Why had the Egyptian's master left him behind?", options:["Because three days agone he fell sick","Because he had stolen spoil","Because he was too slow","Because he had betrayed them"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 30:13",verse:"And David said unto him, To whom belongest thou? and whence art thou? And he said, I am a young man of Egypt, servant to an Amalekite; and my master left me, because three days agone I fell sick.", insight:"His master left him when he fell sick; the world's loyalty lasts only while you are useful."},
{q:"What did the Egyptian ask of David before guiding him?", options:["Swear unto me by God, that thou wilt neither kill me, nor deliver me to my master","Gold and silver as payment","Freedom for his family","A place among David's men"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 30:15",verse:"And David said to him, Canst thou bring me down to this company? And he said, Swear unto me by God, that thou wilt neither kill me, nor deliver me into the hands of my master, and I will bring thee down to this company.", insight:"He asked an oath for his life; mercy given freely returns as loyalty freely offered."},
{q:"What were the Amalekites doing when David found them?", options:["Eating and drinking, and dancing, because of all the great spoil","Sleeping in their tents","Sacrificing to their gods","Marching to battle"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 30:16",verse:"And when he had brought him down, behold, they were spread abroad upon all the earth, eating and drinking, and dancing, because of all the great spoil that they had taken out of the land of the Philistines, and out of the land of Judah.", insight:"They were dancing over their spoil; pride feasts loudest just before the fall."},
{q:"How long did David smite the Amalekites?", options:["From the twilight even unto the evening of the next day","For seven days","For forty days","Until the third watch"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 30:17",verse:"And David smote them from the twilight even unto the evening of the next day: and there escaped not a man of them, save four hundred young men, which rode upon camels, and fled.", insight:"From twilight to the evening of the next day; thorough obedience leaves no enemy standing."},
{q:"What did David recover from the Amalekites?", options:["All that they had carried away, and his two wives","Only the flocks and herds","Half of the spoil","The women, but not the goods"], a:0, ref:"1 Samuel 30:18",verse:"And David recovered all that the Amalekites had carried away: and David rescued his two wives.", insight:"David recovered all; what God promises to restore, He restores completely."}
]}]);
